{
  "task": "Investigate parked-car jagged blue/red patches; no fix, no PR",
  "baseCommit": "2d6e0465e",
  "finding": "The sedan texture-to-flat-vertex-colour conversion creates the jagged glass, grille and lamp boundaries. These are opaque material-colour regions on the car surface, not torn baked shadows.",
  "controls": {
    "originalSource": "Original Meshy sedan own-texture emission renders have clean window, grille and lamp contours, four angles.",
    "derivedUnlit": "Derived runtime sedan with native vertex RGB and alpha-controlled white repaint reproduces the triangular teeth in Blender, four angles, no lights or Godot lightmap.",
    "plainUnlit": "Replacing only the same mesh appearance with a constant opaque white emission removes the marks, four angles.",
    "gamePlain": "Named temporary car_model_material control swaps the shared vehicle material for a plain lit material. Same camera, car meshes, shadows and 0.31 lightmap. Glass/grille/lamp teeth disappear; native shader restoration reproduces identical PNG bytes.",
    "lightingToggles": "Not performed, following user instruction to do them only if the standalone model is clean."
  },
  "causeDetails": [
    "tools/assets/build-faceted-models.py finish_meshy samples and clusters the source albedo, split_by_colour assigns one colour per triangle/subtriangle and stops at depth=2 for sedan. Geometry triangles span texture material boundaries, so the derived colour contours follow triangle edges.",
    "The final COLOR_0 alpha is 1 only on the blue body cluster and 0 on glass/trim/red lamps. vehicle_paint.gdshader correctly replaces alpha=1 with per-car paint, retaining the ragged alpha=0 colours.",
    "Both runtime vehicles have zero textures/images and no TEXCOORD_0, so runtime atlas bleeding, broken texture UVs and wrong texture assignment cannot produce these marks.",
    "The sedan has 6745 triangles, zero degenerate triangles, zero reversed normals, and identical RGBA at all three corners of every triangle. Its source hash and derived hash match committed provenance.",
    "The red patch is a jagged taillamp region; the dark blue shapes correspond to glass/grille/trim, which the game lights tint cool.",
    "The current van is the approved Hunyuan reduction, not Meshy. It was also rendered with its own source maps and native/white/plain runtime colours from four angles."
  ],
  "smallestProposedFix": "Keep the current sedan silhouette and placement. Correct only its generated colour/paint-mask boundaries at glass, grille and lamps: split triangles along clean material-region contours and assign COLOR_0 RGB/alpha consistently on each side; regenerate sedan.glb.bin and its provenance/derived metadata. This retains flat colours instead of hiding the issue by whitening every surface. Increasing subdivision depth may reduce jaggedness but does not guarantee clean boundaries. No change implemented.",
  "limitations": [
    "Supplied montage does not record original camera transform. Captures reproduce the marks and street framing with documented free-camera positions, rather than claiming pixel-identical original viewpoint.",
    "Van audit found 318 normals opposing geometric triangle winding, a separate reduction issue; the implicated sedan has none. No geometry repair performed.",
    "Cold-cache launch logged D3D12 pipeline creation warnings and live-arena fallback while warming. The rendered captures completed, and StudyLightmap reported static:1380, probeOnly:423, environmentOnly:1113.",
    "Plain material is a diagnostic control removing all vehicle colour detail, not the proposed production appearance."
  ],
  "engine": "GodotJS 4.6.1, D3D12 Forward+, AMD Radeon RX 9070 XT",
  "capturePixels": [
    1920,
    1080
  ],
